**§ 1º O** The Periodic Expenditure Review Plan shall contain:

I – a multi-year public expenditure framework, distributed according to government functions;

II – an assessment of the economic viability and fiscal sustainability of public policies and government programs, jointly, and of the most relevant public policies and programs, individually, including tax waivers and incentives;

III – the fiscal impact of mandatory expenditures;

IV – measures necessary to enhance fiscal management and public policies, particularly those aimed at eradicating poverty and marginalization and reducing social and regional inequalities, including a priority legislative agenda;

V – identification of budget-saving options to reduce the fiscal deficit or create fiscal space for more prioritized programs, especially those focused on economic and social development.

**§ 2** The Periodic Expenditure Review Plan shall present the reference fiscal scenario and the measures necessary to achieve and maintain public account balance in the short, medium, and long term.

**§ 3º O** The reference fiscal scenario mentioned in § 2 shall:

I – contain fiscal projections for revenues and expenditures, for periods of 3 (three), 10 (ten), and 20 (twenty) years;

