Article 1. A special pension is granted, in accordance with this Law, to legal dependents of those who have requested the amnesty provided for in Law No. 8,878 of May 11, 1994, and who have passed away before the completion of their respective administrative proceedings. Art. 2º For the purposes of this Law, legal dependents are those entitled to apply for a death pension under the social security system to which the individuals referred to in Article 1 of this Law would have been integrated if the request for amnesty had been granted. Article 3. The grant of the benefit provided for in Article 1 of this Law shall be subject to the following requirements:
       I - It shall depend on a request by the interested parties;
       II - The request shall only be approved if, after examining the factual situation contained therein, it is determined that there was a right to the grant of amnesty, in accordance with Law No. 8,878 of May 11, 1994;
       III - The calculation of the benefit shall follow the specific rules of the pension regime to which the deceased would have been integrated if the amnesty had been granted, considering his hypothetical enrollment in the system without retroactive effects. Art. 4 The granting of the benefit provided for in this Law will depend on the establishment of specific budget provisions. Art. 5
This Law shall enter into force on the date of its publication.

